    "durationMs": 293685,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Laravel 11.57.1 on PHP 8.3, with Eloquent persistence on the provided MySQL 8.4 (`/workspace` now holds the full project, vendor installed, no `.env` so the real `DB_*` environment is the single source of truth).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `links` table migration: unique 20-char `code` (case-sensitive `utf8mb4_bin`), `text url` stored unchanged, `clicks` counter.\n- `LinkController` with the four actions; routes registered without any prefix or middleware group via `withRouting(then:)` in `bootstrap/app.php` (no CSRF, no throttling).\n- Validation: `url` required, absolute http/https with a host (custom closure rule); `code` optional, `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`; generated codes via `Str::random(8)` with uniqueness check plus a DB unique-index fallback that returns 409 on races.\n- Global JSON error rendering in `bootstrap/app.php`: 422 for validation/malformed JSON (Laravel decodes broken JSON to empty input → \"url required\"), 404 JSON for unknown routes/links — all with an `error` field, regardless of `Accept` header.\n- `start.sh`: `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground. I confirmed in the ServeCommand source that without `--no-reload`, Laravel strips all non-passthrough env vars from the server child process — with it, the full `$_ENV` (including `DB_*`) passes through.\n- README documents startup and every endpoint.\n\n**Verification** — ran the full matrix against the live server started by `sh start.sh`: 201 creates (generated + custom codes, URL returned byte-identical including userinfo/port/query/fragment), 409 duplicate code, 422 for every bad url/code/malformed-JSON case, 200 list in creation order with `items`/`total`, 200 show, 404 unknown codes, 302 with exact `Location`, and clicks incrementing exactly once per redirect. I then restarted the server: migrations were idempotent and all data plus click counts survived in MySQL. Test server is stopped and port 8000 is free."
